,"қас"],"answerKk":"бұйра"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"spiky","options":["торчащий, ёжиком","второй подбородок","полный, с лишним весом","крепкого сложения","стройный"],"answer":"торчащий, ёжиком","optionsKk":["тікенді","қос иек","артық салмақты","қапсағай","сымбатты"],"answerKk":"тікенді"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"straight","options":["прямой","загадочный","самоописанный","носить (одежду)","идти, быть к лицу"],"answer":"прямой","optionsKk":["тік","жұмбақ","өзі сипаттаған","кию","жарасу"],"answerKk":"тік"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"shoulder-length","options":["до плеч","описание","чёлка","усы","щетина"],"answer":"до плеч","optionsKk":["иыққа дейін","сипаттама","шаш кекілі","мұрт","қырынбаған сақал"],"answerKk":"иыққа дейін"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"The strangers&rsquo; descriptions were <span class=\"hl\">far more positive</span>."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"Her own version was <span class=\"hl\">not nearly as</span> accurate <span class=\"hl\">as</span> his."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It is <span class=\"hl\">by far the least</span> reliable description available."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"","prompt":"Which of the first three shows the smallest difference?","options":["the first — a bit","the second — much","the third — far","they are all the same size"],"answer":"the first — a bit"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"Listen to five sentences. Which modifier do you hear?","prompt":"The descriptions were … more positive. ____","options":["(no modifier)","much","far","a bit"],"answer":"much"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"Listen to five sentences. Which modifier do you hear?","prompt":"The descriptions were … more positive. ____","options":["(no modifier)","much","far","a bit"],"answer":"far"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"Her hair is ____ than her sister’s.","options":["more curly","curlier","more curlier"],"answer":"curlier"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"The strangers’ descriptions were far ____ .","options":["more positive","positiver","most positive"],"answer":"more positive"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"He’s ____ his brother.","options":["as tall than","so tall as","as tall as"],"answer":"as tall as"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Choose the correct form.","prompt":"It’s ____ reliable description available.","options":["the least by far more","by far the least","far the less"],"answer":"by far the least"},{"stage":"Listening","type":"listen","title":"Why did the writer write this text?","prompt":"The writer wrote this text mainly to","options":["recommend the advertisement","use a famous film to examine how differently we describe ourselves and others","explain how forensic artists work"],"answer":"use a famous film to examine how differently we describe ourselves and others","track":"Track_9.1.mp3"},{"stage":"Listening","type":"rows","title":"True, False, or Not Given?","sub":"","track":"Track_9.1.mp3","items":[{"q":"The artist could see the women he was drawing.","options":["True","False","Not Given"],"answer":"False"},{"q":"The self-described portraits were usually less flattering.","options":["True","False","Not Given"],"answer":"True"}]},{"stage":"Listening","type":"rows","title":"Read quickly. Choose the best heading for each paragraph.","sub":"","track":"Track_9.1.mp3","items":[{"q":"A Paragraph A ____","options":["An unusual set-up","Two faces, side by side","Why the film worked, and what it was not","What the research actually shows","A question of how much you look","What is left when the advertising ends"